_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 13
---
order: 13
---
short_label: X.13
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two magnitudes are commensurable, and one of them is incommensurable with any magnitude, then the remaining one is also incommensurable with the same.
----
proof:

Let *A* and *B* be two commensurable magnitudes, and let one of them, *A,* be incommensurable with some other magnitude *C.*

I say that the remaining one, *B,* is also incommensurable with *C.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="120" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.13 diagram" src="propX13.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.13",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "B0;point;free;-1000,65;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;1000,65;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,100;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,100;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,170,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,30,0;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,200,0;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,30,0;0",
            "C2;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,150,0;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

If *B* is commensurable with *C,* while *A* is also commensurable with *B,* then *A* is also commensurable with *C.* [!just X.12]

But it is also incommensurable with it, which is impossible. Therefore *B* is not commensurable with *C.* Therefore it is incommensurable with it.

Therefore, *if two magnitudes are commensurable, and one of them is incommensurable with any magnitude, then the remaining one is also incommensurable with the same.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: The proposition is a logical variant of the previous. It is used in very frequently in Book X starting with @X.18.
